Nice — below is a complete, practical plan plus ready-to-run code snippets to convert the Thymeleaf UI into a React single-page application (SPA) backed by the same Spring Boot backend exposed as REST endpoints.

I’ll give you:

Required backend changes (REST controllers + CORS).

REST endpoints (URLs, request / response shapes).

A React app structure and full code for key components (using create-react-app).

How to run both backend and frontend locally (dev mode).

Extensions (notifications, authentication) suggestions.

If you're on Spring Boot 3 / Jakarta, make sure you use jakarta.persistence.* imports and Java records as shown 

(or regular DTO classes if on older Java).

CORS note

I used @CrossOrigin(origins = "http://localhost:3000") to allow React dev server calls. In production, configure CORS more securely.



